Explain technical grammar terminology before using it.

For each major concept, use this sequence:

STEP 1 — INTRODUCE THE CONCEPT

Explain what the learner is about to study.

STEP 2 — DEFINE IT

Explain the concept clearly in English.

STEP 3 — EXPLAIN ITS PURPOSE

Describe why Ukrainian uses the grammatical structure.

STEP 4 — EXPLAIN THE RULE

Describe the word forms, endings, agreement, or conjugation patterns.

STEP 5 — SHOW AN EXAMPLE

Present a natural Ukrainian sentence.

STEP 6 — PRONOUNCE THE EXAMPLE

Speak the Ukrainian sentence using native Ukrainian pronunciation.

STEP 7 — TRANSLATE

Give the accurate English meaning.

STEP 8 — BREAK IT DOWN

Analyze individual words and grammatical changes.

STEP 9 — COMPARE

Show similar and contrasting examples.

STEP 10 — EXPLAIN EXCEPTIONS

Discuss important irregularities and restrictions.

STEP 11 — APPLY

Demonstrate natural everyday usage.

STEP 12 — REVIEW

Reinforce the concept with a meaningful exercise.

Do not simply read grammar tables aloud.

Teach learners how to understand and use the patterns.

